# What does NOT go in the plugin the directory serves.
#
# The zip somebody installs is not the repository. It holds what the plugin
# needs to RUN — the PHP, the built admin bundle, the vendored libraries, the
# translations — and nothing about how it is developed. Shipping the rest is not
# only weight: every file in the package is a file the review team reads, a file
# a security scanner reports on, and a file somebody can request over HTTP.
#
# Read by `npm run package`, which is what builds the zip. The format is one
# path fragment per line, the same as WP-CLI's `wp dist-archive`.

# --- version control and CI --------------------------------------------------

.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.husky
.distignore
.editorconfig

# --- the source the build is made from ---------------------------------------
#
# src/ AND the build config SHIP, which is not the obvious choice. The directory
# requires that compiled code be accompanied by human-readable source, and the
# usual answer is a link to a repository — but src/ is 576K against vendor's
# 4.5M, so carrying it costs about a tenth of the package and turns the
# strongest objection a reviewer can raise into nothing to discuss. The webpack
# and Tailwind configs go with it so the build is reproducible rather than
# merely readable.
#
# node_modules and the lockfile do not. The lockfile is larger than the source
# it locks, and neither is needed to read or rebuild.

node_modules
package-lock.json

# --- development tooling -----------------------------------------------------

composer.json
composer.lock
phpcs.xml.dist
phpcs.xml
.php-cs-fixer.dist.php
.php-cs-fixer.php
.php-cs-fixer.cache
.phpunit.result.cache
.eslintrc.js
.eslintignore
.prettierrc
.prettierignore

# --- the suite and the scripts -----------------------------------------------
#
# tests/ stubs WordPress by declaring its functions in the global namespace,
# which is correct in a test harness and alarming in a plugin. bin/ is release
# machinery. Neither runs on a site.

tests
bin

# --- the directory listing, rather than the plugin ---------------------------
#
# The icon, banner and screenshots belong to SVN's own assets/ directory, which
# is a SIBLING of trunk/ rather than part of it. Shipping them would send a
# megabyte of marketing to every site on every update. See assets/README.md.

assets

# --- writing about the plugin, rather than the plugin ------------------------
#
# readme.txt ships, because that IS the directory listing. LICENSE ships, because
# the GPL requires the licence to travel with the work and the directory expects
# to find it. The rest is written for somebody reading the repository, and would
# otherwise turn up inside a stranger's WordPress admin.

README.md
CHANGELOG.md
CONTRIBUTING.md

# --- generated at runtime ----------------------------------------------------

generated

# --- what this script itself produces ----------------------------------------
#
# A previous release sitting in the working directory. Without this the second
# run packages the first run's zip inside the new one, which doubles the size
# and is not obviously wrong from the outside.

schemapress.*.zip

# --- operating systems -------------------------------------------------------

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
